        "text": "Install the Framework in a Scratch Org Set up your environment. The Trailhead project Quick Start: Salesforce DX  shows these steps: Enable Dev Hub in your org or Trailhead Playground. Install Visual Studio Code . Install the Salesforce CLI . Install the Salesforce extensions for Visual Studio Code . Authorize your Dev Hub org, if you did not do it before, and give it an alias(myhuborg  in this command): sf org login web --set-default-dev-hub --alias myhuborg Clone the salesforce-trigger-framework repository: git clone https://github.com/dschach/salesforce-trigger-framework cd salesforce-trigger-framework Create your scratch org. Use the script or the Salesforce CLI. With the script: Note:  The script first deletes the scratch org with the alias TriggerFramework , if there is one. Then it creates a new scratch org with that alias, deploys the framework and the sample handler, and opens the org. In the terminal of Visual Studio Code, run the orginit script : bash scripts/orginit.sh With the Salesforce CLI: Create an empty scratch org and give it an alias(triggerHandler  in this command): sf org create scratch --set-default --definition-file config/project-scratch-def.json --alias triggerHandler Deploy the framework to your scratch org. To deploy the sample handler and trigger too, add --source-dir sample-handler : sf project deploy start --source-dir force-app Open the scratch org: sf org open"
