        "title": "AccountSampleTriggerHandler",
        "fileName": "AccountSampleTriggerHandler.html",
        "text": "AccountSampleTriggerHandler A sample Account trigger handler that shows how to use the framework. Before insert and before update, it removes extra spaces from each new or changed Account name. After update, it copies a changed phone number to the child Accounts. It bypasses itself for that update, so the update does not run this handler again. A loop limit stops recursion that the bypass does not stop. andFinally()  runs after each context. A trigger runs without sharing, so this inherited sharing  handler does too. Each query and DML statement names SYSTEM_MODE , so the handler can update child Accounts that the running user cannot edit. Signature public inherited sharing class AccountSampleTriggerHandler extends TriggerHandler See AccountSampleTriggerHandlerTest Author David Schach Since 2021 2026-10 Rewrite the sample to show the framework in use AccountSampleTriggerHandler Properties Name Signature Annotations Description finishedOperations private static List<System.TriggerOperation> finishedOperations @TestVisible The trigger operations that this handler finished in the transaction, in order. andFinally()  adds each one. MAX_LOOP_COUNT private static final Integer MAX_LOOP_COUNT The maximum number of runs of each trigger operation of this handler in 1 transaction. Each chunk of 200 records uses 1 run. So 50 allows an update of 10,000 records, which runs before update and after update 50 times each. newRecords private List<Account> newRecords The new Accounts of the trigger, cast from Trigger.new . oldRecordsMap private Map<Id, Account> oldRecordsMap The old Accounts of the trigger by Id, cast from Trigger.oldMap . It is null in an insert. AccountSampleTriggerHandler Constructors AccountSampleTriggerHandler() Creates the handler for the trigger. It passes its class to the base class, so the base class does no name lookup. It casts the trigger collections that the handler uses, and it sets the loop limit. AccountSampleTriggerHandler() Creates the handler for the trigger. It passes its class to the base class, so the base class does no name lookup. It casts the trigger collections that the handler uses, and it sets the loop limit. Signature public AccountSampleTriggerHandler() Example new AccountSampleTriggerHandler().run(); AccountSampleTriggerHandler Methods afterUpdate() Copies each changed phone number to the child Accounts. andFinally() Records the finished operation. A real handler puts work here that must follow each context, for example a rollup. andFinally()  runs after each context. For an insert, an update, or a delete, it runs 2 times for each chunk of 200 records. It runs after the before context and again after the after context. Some work must run only once for each chunk, for example the publication of 1 platform event. Put that work in an if  block that checks getTriggerEvent()  for an after context. beforeInsert() Removes extra spaces from the name of each new Account. beforeUpdate() Removes extra spaces from each Account name that changed. copyPhoneToChildAccounts(phoneByParentId) Updates the phone number of the child Accounts. The handler is bypassed for that update. It leaves out a child Account that is in the same trigger run, because a trigger cannot update the records that it runs for. The query and the update run in system mode, so this method suppresses FlagSystemMode . The phone number must reach all child Accounts, also the ones that the running user cannot see or edit. normalizeNames(accounts) Replaces each group of spaces in the Account names with 1 space, and removes the spaces at the start and the end. afterUpdate() Copies each changed phone number to the child Accounts. Signature public override void afterUpdate() andFinally() Records the finished operation. A real handler puts work here that must follow each context, for example a rollup. andFinally()  runs after each context. For an insert, an update, or a delete, it runs 2 times for each chunk of 200 records. It runs after the before context and again after the after context. Some work must run only once for each chunk, for example the publication of 1 platform event. Put that work in an if  block that checks getTriggerEvent()  for an after context. Signature public override void andFinally() Since 2026-10 Example // andFinally() runs after the before context and again after the after context. // This example runs only once for each chunk of 200 records, after the after context. public override void andFinally() { if(getTriggerEvent() == System.TriggerOperation.AFTER_UPDATE) { EventBus.publish(new Account_Change__e(Record_Count__c = Trigger.size)); } } beforeInsert() Removes extra spaces from the name of each new Account. Signature public override void beforeInsert() beforeUpdate() Removes extra spaces from each Account name that changed. Signature public override void beforeUpdate() copyPhoneToChildAccounts(phoneByParentId) Updates the phone number of the child Accounts. The handler is bypassed for that update. It leaves out a child Account that is in the same trigger run, because a trigger cannot update the records that it runs for. The query and the update run in system mode, so this method suppresses FlagSystemMode . The phone number must reach all child Accounts, also the ones that the running user cannot see or edit. Signature @SuppressWarnings('PMD.FlagSystemMode') private void copyPhoneToChildAccounts(Map<Id, String> phoneByParentId) Parameters phoneByParentId Type: Map<Id, String> The new phone number of each parent Account, by Id. Since 2026-10 normalizeNames(accounts) Replaces each group of spaces in the Account names with 1 space, and removes the spaces at the start and the end. Signature private static void normalizeNames(List<Account> accounts) Parameters accounts Type: List<Account> The Accounts to change. Since 2026-10"
